ight after that but goku quickly  resumes blue form and sends an attack  that catches granola off guard granola  tests out if it was a fluke but goku  keeps shifting his vitals out of harm's  way and can actually land hits on  granola that sent him flying back  granola still feels confident for his  part though since with this strategy  goku is mainly on the defensive and he  can't see goku being able to launch  attacks that can take him out and goku  himself admits that this could be a  problem with the smile on his face  absolutely love how goku meets  challenges like this with a smile on his  face rather than with frustration vegeta  then comes to and witnesses some  exchanging of blows between goku and  granola but it seems to be of no use  granola lands a hit and afterwards goku  reverts to his base form once again  surprisingly early in his turn goku  acknowledges that his body won't last  much longer and shockingly vegeta  confidently asserts that he's tagging in  and he actually looks up to it based on  his expression that is vegeta blames his  saiyan pride for his stubbornness and  desire to win alone and mentions that  since granola just learned to unleash  this side of his power he won't last  long and granola actually does look  really tired even more so than vegeta at  the moment vegeta is banking on granola  hitting his limit and he'll take  advantage of it when it happens and go  for the win goku agrees and just tells  vegeta not to die for us vegeta fans who  want to see vegeta get the w here  there's definitely been plenty of vegeta  greatness already and great to see him  coming in once more and getting another  chance to win this this has definitely  been his battle more than goku so far  and i honestly would love it to stay  that way but we'll see what happens  vegeta then starts playing with granola  mentally stating that his drive for  revenge has rotted his brain he thinks  he's only alive for revenge and that  there's nothing more to live for one of  the reasons vegeta can read granola so  well is because he was also in the same  boat in the past whether he wanted  revenge against frieza or goku he can  probably imagine exactly what granola is  thinking vegeta even eggs granola on  asking him to hit him with everything he  can muster and then once more he  transforms to ultra eagle vegeta i'm as  surprised as granola that vegeta can  keep this up but i'm definitely not  complaining granola says vegeta's hit  his limit but vegeta reiterates that  this power is unbounded and has no  limits vegeta is now definitely the one  on the offensive and as he hits granola  close to the city granola begs to take  the battle elsewhere showing that he  clearly isn't that single-mindedly  focused on revenge as he thought since  he's still trying to protect the city  and the civilians you gotta love how  vegeta even resorts to chomping down on  granola's arm that he was using to try  and punch him not exactly refined  martial arts technique but fun to see  vegeta go so animalistic vegeta reveals  that he's been strategic and brought him  to the city so that granola couldn't use  his rapid fire attacks however in such  close range he's sure the city will be  fine and he unleashes point blank  attacks at vegeta despite what he  thought the attacks did reach some  buildings as they begin to crack vegeta  is in base form again and even granola  has reverted to a previous form as his  second eye is back to normal and he's  panting like he's about to drop any  second as he lays down to rest for a  second the window behind him cracks  revealing some traumatized citizens  granola is beginning to realize that  he's in a way become like the saiyans  that destroyed his own city despite the  motive his battle is leading to a  repetition of history and this time he's  not the victim we see a really cute kid  granola running to his pretty mother in  a flashback as they embrace suddenly  something frightens them and it's  implied that she died thanks to  destruction caused by the saiyans now  just as he was cowering in fear with his  mom he sees these new sugarians doing  the same and this time he's brought on  their fear vegeta bless him gets up  again this dude has been extraordinary  this arc he really has and he's sounding  pretty rational here he says that the  grudges against the saiyans are well  deserved and he won't object to granola  destroying him but wouldn't granola  eradicating the saiyans just be  repeating history so vegeta has pretty  much said what we've been observing  history is clearly repeating itself with  all the destruction and innocent people  suffering again thanks to granola's  fight against the saiyans granola tries  to hold on though to his revenge and  screams that their planet was always  peaceful and then the saiyans took  everything from him so he can't move  past that ever he unleashes more damage  on vegeta now vegeta must be in really  bad shape and to make matters worse  granola is ready to burn away the rest  of his life force here aka he'll shave  his remaining life and put it into a  super powerful attack for us it's so  obvious how stupid this is frieza is the  only one who may deserve this attack and  yet granola is going to use it on  frieza's enemies before he ever even  gets a chance to get revenge on frieza  but it serves to show us how blinding a  thirst for revenge can be especially  when it's this blind and poorly  calculated for instance in the katamati  crystal the revenge is much more  satisfying and well planned here  granolas is poorly planned and more  hysterical than anything else his attack  looks huge and powerful though  definitely enough to finish vegeta off  again he says his revenge on frieza will  have to wait for the afterlife which  shows how ridiculous his whole mission  is as he prepares to meet his death  vegeta isn't afraid or angry he handles  it like a boss smiling and even  apologizing to lord beerus that he  wasn't able to cut it he's willing to  accept this as the fate of the saiyans  if it must be like this and although  this seems to be a contradiction to his  i am the master of my fate line it's not  really in the sense that vegeta is  choosing how to act in the face of death  and to meet it head on rather than  kicking and screaming and resisting it  no one has 100 control over external  events or what happens to them but they  do have control over how they react to  what happens and you can see that in  practice here with vegeta and he's  definitely acting like a boss goku  realizes that they are both willing to  die and wants to stop them and then  granola's namekian friend appears he's  shocked to see goku and that will be  explained pretty soon the namekian sees  the insanely powered up attack and  finally he tells granol to knock it off  granola is shocked to see his friend and  for a second it knocks him out of his  revenge obsessed mind state long enough  for goku to tackle him thus again goku  saves his bro vegeta and you gotta love  vegeta's reaction goku just saved his  life and all he gets is a smirk and  from vegeta in the meantime granola is  mad at monato for interfering and you  can see that granola is tormented the  search for revenge as a life's purpose  is clearly not a happy way to exist in  utter anguish he screams out that he  just wants it to end he needs it to be  over finally monaeto drops the most  shocking thing of the chapter he  explains that granola can't generalize  with saiyans because even then there was  one saiyan who didn't earn his vengeance  40 years ago the one who saved them was  bardock we all know as goku's dad and  then a shocked granola repeats that  hussein was actually their savior  showing just how idiotic and  oversimplified granola's revenge against  all saiyans was but i think for all of  us we're just so excited to see bardock  being brought back into the story  bardock is some of my favorite dragon  ball material and i did not expect them  to be brought into this arc but we may  well get some bardock flashback now and  i cannot be happier about that first  vegeta's amazing new form and now  bardock this arc of dragon ball super is  amazing in my view and i'm enjoying it  much more than the moral arc personally  but as always let me know your thoughts  on this chapter and what you are most  looking forward to happening next for me  it's definitely bardock and let me know  who your mvp was this chapter if you're  asking me it had to be vegeta for just  constantly getting up time after time  and for the way he was ready to  stoically accept his own end vegeta has  been glorious this arc no doubt anyways  if you do enjoy seeing these dragon ball  super reviews and want to keep them  coming you know what to do channel the  super saiyan within and smash that like  button with no mercy remember that  smashing is goku energy and passing is  yamcha energy so choose wisely if you  haven't make this the video you  subscribe and this is crucial hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications or you will miss future  dragon ball super videos and updates and  until next time see ya space cowboys  [Music]  so  [Music]

